swehouse.c: Krusinski returns zero for eight of its twelve cusp speeds

Cusps 1, 4, 7 and 10 come out right because the generic code before the switch
has already filled them. Case 'U' never writes the other eight, so they keep
the zero swe_houses_armc_ex2() left in the array.

    swetest -b1.1.2000 -ut12:00 -house13.4,52.5,U -speed

      house  2   67  5 24.2693     0  0  0.0000   ->  539 23 16.9198
      house  3   83 56  9.7029     0  0  0.0000   ->  453  5 58.5360
      house  5  165 40 43.0836     0  0  0.0000   ->  456 43 47.9608
      house  6  209 34  8.6725     0  0  0.0000   ->  624 36 53.1067

and the same for 8, 9, 11 and 12. Berlin, J2000, nothing polar about it; the
eight zeros are there at every latitude I tried.

The cusps come out of a chain of rotations rather than a closed formula, but
the chain still differentiates. Only armc and the Ascendant move, and
swe_cotrans_sp() already carries a velocity along with its position, so the
rotations need no differencing; the two ecliptic-to-equator conversions are
differentiated directly.

Positions do not change. Checked against a Richardson extrapolated difference
of the cusp positions over 25,520 dates between 1000 BC and 4100 AD, at random
latitudes and longitudes, every date judged rather than a subsample: mean
relative error 6.665e-01 before, 2.365e-10 after. The remaining 2e-10 is the
differencing reference's own floor, not the formula's; the worst single point
is 9.9e-08, at a cusp moving 1.1 degrees a day where a relative error means
little.

---
 swehouse.c | 50 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 50 insertions(+)
diff --git a/swehouse.c b/swehouse.c
index d48d026..5b38151 100644
--- a/swehouse.c
+++ b/swehouse.c
@@ -2002,6 +2002,56 @@ porphyry:
       hsp->cusp[i+1] = swe_degnorm(hsp->cusp[i+1]);
       hsp->cusp[i+7] = swe_degnorm(hsp->cusp[i+1]+180);
     }
+    /* The cusps come out of a chain of rotations rather than a closed
+     * formula, but the chain is still differentiable. Only two things move:
+     * armc itself, and the Ascendant, which enters through its right
+     * ascension and its declination.
+     *   u    = RA(ac) - (th - 90)
+     *   kr   = longitude of (u, dec(ac)) rotated by -(90 - fi)
+     *   RA_i = longitude of (30i, 0) rotated by 90, shifted by kr, rotated
+     *          by (90 - fi), plus (th - 90)
+     *   cusp = ecliptic longitude having right ascension RA_i
+     * The two rotations are carried by swe_cotrans_sp(), which moves a
+     * velocity along with its position, so nothing here is differenced; the
+     * ecliptic/equator conversions are differentiated in closed form
+     * through dRA/dlon = cos(eps) / (cos^2 lon + cos^2 eps sin^2 lon).
+     * The singular direction enters only through ac_speed, which is
+     * AscDash()'s and is already correct at the horizon tangency. */
+    if (hsp->do_hspeed) {
+      double de, dde, u, du, kr, dkr, wac;
+      double xa[6];
+      xa[0] = hsp->ac; xa[1] = 0.0; xa[2] = 1.0;
+      swe_cotrans(xa, xa, -ekl);
+      de = xa[1];
+      wac = cosd(hsp->ac) * cosd(hsp->ac) + cose * cose * sind(hsp->ac) * sind(hsp->ac);
+      dde = cosd(hsp->ac) * sine / cosd(de) * hsp->ac_speed;
+      u = swe_degnorm(xa[0] - (th - 90));
+      du = cose / wac * hsp->ac_speed - ARMCS;
+      {
+	/* swe_cotrans_sp() rotates a position and its velocity together, so the
+	 * rotation needs no differencing: hand it (u, de) moving at (du, dde) and
+	 * read the rotated longitude and its rate straight back out. */
+	double xb[6];
+	xb[0] = u; xb[1] = de; xb[2] = 1.0;
+	xb[3] = du; xb[4] = dde; xb[5] = 0.0;
+	swe_cotrans_sp(xb, xb, -(90 - fi));
+	kr = xb[0];
+	dkr = xb[3];
+      }
+      for (i = 0; i < 6; i++) {
+	double xc[6], dRAi, wc;
+	xc[0] = 30.0 * i; xc[1] = 0.0; xc[2] = 1.0;
+	xc[3] = 0.0; xc[4] = 0.0; xc[5] = 0.0;
+	swe_cotrans_sp(xc, xc, 90);
+	xc[0] += kr; xc[3] = dkr;
+	swe_cotrans_sp(xc, xc, 90 - fi);
+	dRAi = xc[3] + ARMCS;
+	wc = cosd(hsp->cusp[i+1]) * cosd(hsp->cusp[i+1])
+	   + cose * cose * sind(hsp->cusp[i+1]) * sind(hsp->cusp[i+1]);
+	hsp->cusp_speed[i+1] = dRAi * wc / cose;
+	hsp->cusp_speed[i+7] = hsp->cusp_speed[i+1];
+      }
+    }
     break;
   case 'Y':     /* APC houses */
     for (i = 1; i <= 12; i++) {
